  "description": "Intraoperative recordings from 16 people with Parkinson's disease performing a grip-force task during bilateral subthalamic nucleus (STN) deep brain stimulation lead implantation. Each run includes subdural ECoG over sensorimotor cortex, STN local field potentials, and grip-force channels. The data were used to compare electrocorticography with subthalamic LFPs for movement decoding. This BIDS derivative reorganizes the 1 kHz resampled signals released on Harvard Dataverse.",
  "methods_description": "Signals were recorded intraoperatively with a Ripple Grapevine system (filtered 0.3-7.5 kHz, digitised at 30 kHz) and resampled to 1 kHz. Recordings comprise a subdural ECoG strip, four STN DBS lead contacts, and bilateral grip-force traces, with noise- and drift-cleaned force versions also provided.",
